            {
                "box": {
                    "id": "obj-33",
                    "linecount": 60,
                    "maxclass": "comment",
                    "numinlets": 1,
                    "numoutlets": 0,
                    "patching_rect": [ 30.0, 553.0, 579.0, 885.0 ],
                    "text": "================================================================================\nheterodyne_pd_shaper — Parameter Information\n================================================================================\n\nOVERVIEW\nImplements General-Purpose Heterodyne Phase Distortion (PD) from Lazzarini, Timoney, Pekonen, and Välimäki (DAFx-09 Paper 12, Section 3.2 & 4.2, Eq. 5–6, 17, Fig. 9, 17–20). Places the arbitrary stereo tuba signal in quadrature (s_re, s_im) via a 4-stage IIR Hilbert network and ring-modulates it with the cosine and sine of a pitch-tracked Casio CZ-style piecewise phase-distortion function g(phi). Unlike lookup-table PD, this applies true phase distortion across every partial of the live acoustic tuba while allowing the modulation index to exceed the classical pi limit to boost secondary vocal/brass formant regions.\n\nINLETS & OUTLETS\n- in1 / in2: Stereo Audio Input (Full Tuba or 01_harmonic_isolator)\n- in3: Tracked Fundamental Pitch f0 in Hz (from 00_tuba_freq_tracker; falls back to internal zero-crossing tracker if <= 0)\n- in4: Optional 1-Bar Audio-Rate Phasor [0..1] (modulates the inflection point d when mod_depth > 0; internal 0.5 Hz fallback if unpatched)\n- out1 / out2: Stereo Heterodyne Phase-Distorted Output\n\nPARAMETERS (6)\n\n1. pd_ratio\n   - Range: 0.25 to 4.00 (Modulator-to-Fundamental Ratio f_m / f_0)\n   - Taper: Linear ratio (1.0 = classic phase-synchronous PD; 2.0 = octave-doubled formant PD; 0.5 = sub-octave phase inflection).\n   - Function: Scales the frequency of the piecewise phase-distortion modulator relative to the tuba's fundamental pitch.\n\n2. inflection_d\n   - Range: 0.02 to 0.98 (Piecewise Breakpoint Duty Cycle d, Default: 0.15)\n   - Taper: Linear duty ratio centered at 0.50 (no distortion). Moving d toward 0.02 or 0.98 steepens the phase inflection and widens the harmonic bandwidth like opening a lowpass filter.\n   - Function: Sets the horizontal breakpoint where the two linear phase segments meet (DAFx-09 Fig. 1).\n\n3. pd_index\n   - Range: 0.0 to 5.0 (Phase Distortion Index Multiplier, Default: 1.25)\n   - Taper: Power curve (x^1.3) for smooth low-index warmth and aggressive high-index formant multiplication.\n   - Function: Scales the amplitude of the phase-distortion function g(phi). 0.0 is clean bypass, 1.0 reproduces exact Casio CZ Phase Distortion, and values up to 5.0 implement DAFx-09 Section 4.2 (Fig. 17) extended PM index scaling (up to 5*pi rad) to strongly enhance upper brass formants.\n\n4. saw_square\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (0.0 = Single-Inflection Sawtooth PD, 1.0 = Double-Inflection Square/Odd-Harmonic PD)\n   - Taper: Linear crossfade between Eq. 6 and Fig. 18 modulation functions.\n   - Function: Morphs the phase-distortion contour from all-harmonic sawtooth inflection (0.0) to hollow, clarinet/riddim square-wave double inflection (1.0).\n\n5. mod_depth\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (0% to +/-38% Inflection Duty Sweep)\n   - Taper: Linear modulation depth with opposite-polarity stereo offset between Left and Right channels.\n   - Function: Sweeps the inflection breakpoint d in counter-phase stereo using the 1-bar phasor on in4.\n\n6. mix\n   - Range: 0.0 to 1.0 (0% Dry Phase-Aligned Hilbert Carrier to 100% Wet Heterodyne PD)\n   - Taper: Linear crossfade (both Dry and Wet share the exact same Hilbert allpass group delay, preventing comb cancellation in parallel blends).\n   - Function: Balances the dry phase-aligned tuba with the heterodyne phase-distorted signal.\n",
                    "varname": "paraminfo_comment"
                }
            }
